SourceName: v4l2loopback
Section: kernel
SourceDateEpoch: 1750705303
CPE-ID: cpe:/o:v4l2loopback_project:v4l2loopback
Maintainer: Michel Promonet <michel.promonet@free.fr>
Architecture: x86_64
Installed-Size: 143360
Filename: kmod-v4l2loopback_6.12.40.0.13.2-r1_x86_64.ipk
Size: 42763
SHA256sum: 1367e7d845f3825bbc8ed00da3b26a5ce679140b4ca6034e0f6e1a0c3b07f074
Description:  This module allows you to create "virtual video devices".
 Normal (v4l2) applications will read these devices as if
 they were ordinary video devices, but the video will not be
 read from e.g. a capture card but instead it is generated
 by another application. 

